From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:25:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: Add SM6450 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the DPU 8.3 found on SM6450. It is a cut-down DPU 8.1, the one on
SM8450: one VIG and two DMA pipes, four CTLs, three layer mixers of
which only LM_0 has a DSPP and LM_2 and LM_3 pair through MERGE_3D_1,
one DSC encoder, writeback 2, and three interfaces: DP on INTF_0, DSI
on INTF_1 and DP again on INTF_3, which is the second MST stream of
the one DP controller.

The block offsets, interrupts, clock controls and bandwidth limits are
those the downstream display driver describes for the SoC; the blocks
and fields it has no word on are taken from SM8450.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
